A||N||5||Gottico||Drivetrain Problem||||8||
Z||000000||Gottico||11-05-2000||09:28 PM||||I have an 88' Formula with a 5spd and I've got a major problem... While the car runs good while idling and has NO problem reving through the rpm range while the trans is in neutral, I can not accelerate passed 1500 Rpm’s without MAJOR vibration and backfiring in all gears. Tune up done about a month ago (plugs, wires, etc...) The only thing that I have noticed is clutch master cylinder or one of the lines is leaking. I have been refilling it about once every 2 days (about 300 miles of city driving) and I have good clutch pedal pressure.  The clutch is approximately 6 months old. I’m at a loss HELP!!!!! <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gottico (edited 11-06-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Phil||11-05-2000||10:04 PM||||Sounds like ignition -plugs, wires, module, cap, rotor or coil||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||11-05-2000||10:54 PM||||You might also want to check the convertor to see if it is clogged.  A severely restricted exhaust can cuase major drivability problems.  <P>Has the fuel filter been replaced recently?  It might idle OK but be starved for fuel at higher RPM's.  Checking fuel pressure might be worthwhile if the other suggestions don't solve the problem.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-05-2000||10:55 PM||||Sounds like plugged catylitic convertor to me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||prof bobo||11-06-2000||05:13 PM||||Check ECM for codes.  If you find some, follow the diagnostic tree if you wish, but pay careful attention to the Coolant temp sensor -it can cause exactly what you describe if it has gone bad.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||11-06-2000||05:24 PM||||The timing could be off.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||3
